    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316">

                <pb facs="0394" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg380"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/4–447</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Robert W. Baker,
                        Secretary to Mr. Edwin W. Pauley, to the
                        Acting Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Los Angeles</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-04-04">April 4, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Acheson</hi>: Mr. Pauley has asked me to
                    ascertain whether you approve his making the attached statement; and, if you do
                    approve, whether you would care to issue it through the Department of
                        State.<anchor n="63" xml:id="d316-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>As you know, while Mr. Pauley has resigned as the United States Representative on
                    the Allied Commission on Reparations, and as the President’s Personal
                    Representative on reparations matters, he has, at the request of the President
                    and Department of State, agreed to remain as advisor on reparations, subject to
                    the call of the Secretary.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert</hi> W. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Baker</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d316-a1.xml" xpointer="d316-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d316-f1" n="63" xml:id="d316-f1-content">
                <p>Mr. Acheson replied to Mr. Pauley on April 12: “The Department has no objection
                    to the statement which you propose; but I would suggest, however, that you issue
                    it personally.” (740.00119 PW/4–447)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
